            <ArticleTitle>Evaluation and diagnosis of low back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>471-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.pop.2012.06.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The diagnosis of low back pain is complicated by the varying presentations and complex nature of pain and the nonstandardized approach by physicians to clinical decision making. Only a few physicians use evidence-based guidelines to assist with clinical decision making. This article reviews a systematic approach to the evaluation and diagnosis of low back pain.</AbstractText>
